---
import PublicLayout from "../layouts/PublicLayout.astro";
import Waitlist from "../components/Waitlist.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<PublicLayout title="Why Lore — Context and project memory" description="Understand how Lore combines conversation context, searchable history, and reviewable project knowledge.">
  <section class="section page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Why Lore</p><h1>Context for the work in progress. <em>Knowledge for the next session.</em></h1><p class="hero-desc">Lore combines context management and persistent project memory in the local gateway your coding agent uses.</p><a class="button button-primary" href={`${base}docs/install/`}>Install Lore →</a></section>
  <nav class="page-sections section" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#pillars">The approach</a><a href="#landscape">Compare approaches</a><a href="#cost">Costs</a><a href="#portability">Your data</a></nav>
  <section class="section" id="pillars"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Three parts of the same workflow.</h2></div><ol class="workflow"><li><span>01</span><h3>Record</h3><p>Keep conversation history in local SQLite so details can be searched later.</p></li><li><span>02</span><h3>Distill</h3><p>Compress older working context as sessions grow, while recent work remains available to the agent.</p></li><li><span>03</span><h3>Curate</h3><p>Extract project decisions and patterns into knowledge you can review and carry between sessions.</p></li></ol></section>
  <section class="section" id="landscape"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Choose the capabilities your workflow needs.</h2><p>These are categories of tools, not claims about every implementation. Some products combine several approaches.</p></div><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Approach comparison"><table><caption>Questions to ask when evaluating memory and context tools</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Approach</th><th scope="col">Typical focus</th><th scope="col">What to check</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Saved instructions or facts</th><td>Explicit conventions and preferences</td><td>Who maintains them, and how do stale facts get corrected?</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Conversation retrieval</th><td>Finding information in earlier sessions</td><td>Can your agent request the original details when a summary is insufficient?</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Context management</th><td>Keeping a long session within model limits</td><td>What remains available after compression?</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Lore</th><td>Local history, context management, and curated project knowledge</td><td>Does the integration fit your client, provider, and review workflow?</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
  <section class="section" id="context-engine"><span id="depth" class="fragment-anchor" aria-hidden="true"></span><div class="section-heading"><h2>Memory has to reach the current task.</h2><p>Lore manages recent conversation, distilled context, and relevant knowledge together. Its recall tool can search for details beyond the material currently in the prompt.</p></div><a class="text-link" href={`${base}docs/architecture/`}>Explore context management and recall →</a></section>
  <section class="section" id="cost"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Understand the extra work and its cost.</h2><p>Distillation and curation make model calls. Provider pricing, background models, batching support, caching, and your configuration affect the result. Lower costs are not guaranteed for every workload.</p></div><p>Lore includes provider budgets and cost information in the local browser. Configure limits and inspect recorded usage before committing to long sessions.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}docs/configuration/`}>Review configuration and budgets →</a></section>
  <section class="section" id="portability"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Keep a record you can inspect.</h2></div><dl class="capabilities"><div><dt>Local history</dt><dd>Conversations, summaries, knowledge, and embeddings are stored in your local database.</dd></div><div><dt>Git-based knowledge</dt><dd><code>.lore.md</code> holds curated knowledge as reviewable Markdown. It does not export your full conversation history.</dd></div><div><dt>Provider boundaries</dt><dd>Agent and background model requests still use configured providers. Production operational telemetry is documented and can be disabled.</dd></div></dl><a class="text-link" href={`${base}docs/installation-reference/`}>See storage, telemetry, and uninstall details →</a></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Evaluate the evidence in context.</h2><p>The published long-session benchmark covers one recorded session and a simulated compaction comparison. Its setup and limitations matter as much as its scores.</p></div><a class="text-link" href={`${base}docs/benchmark/`}>Read the benchmark methodology →</a></section>
  <span id="team" class="fragment-anchor" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <Waitlist />
</PublicLayout>
